Why that is a real bug and not just a style nit:

- A `DbContext` is not thread-safe and is designed to live for one unit of work. A Singleton outlives every request, so concurrent requests would end up sharing one context — you get "A second operation was started on this context before a previous operation completed," stale change-tracker state, and entities from one request leaking into another's results.
