An alternative design, if the cache and the data access are logically separable, is to keep `OrderCacheService` as a singleton that depends only on a `Scoped`-friendly abstraction resolved per call, but the scope-factory approach above is the standard, well-understood pattern and avoids introducing a layer for its own sake.

