One caveat: if `CalculateTotal` ends up being genuinely complex and you find yourself writing many order-shape variations just to test it, that's a signal it deserves to be its own testable unit (extracted to a method the test can call directly, or a separate calculator class) — but that's a refactor decision, not a reason to mock it now.

