One caveat worth checking: if the service must run continuously rather than complete once, waiting on a single completion task is the wrong model — have it signal after the first iteration the test cares about (a `TaskCompletionSource` set once), or inject a mock of whatever external seam (HTTP/repository/clock) it calls and wait on *that* mock's invocation via its own async completion, rather than waiting for the whole hosted service to stop.

